# Response headers for the static assets this Worker serves. Supported for Workers
# static assets, not only for Pages:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/ (checked 2026-07-24)
#
# Only embed.js is served from here. It is deliberately NOT given a long
# `Cache-Control`: Cloudflare's default for a static asset is
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` with an ETag, so a browser revalidates and
# gets a 304 rather than re-downloading. That revalidation is a request to a static
# asset, which is free and unbilled — while a long max-age would leave readers
# running a months-old embed. A stale embed.js is the failure mode #8 names by
# name: the anti-spam transport fields are frozen by their names, and a cached
# script that predates a change disarms a layer silently, only on the attack path.
#
# Rules here do not apply to responses the Worker generates, so the CORS headers on
# /comments stay in src/cors.ts where they belong.

/embed.js
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
